  "pieces": [
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5b9f38d331175e004f00dd38",
      "background": "#606060",
      "content": "<img src=\"https://codex-content.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/images/1537170585068-bg-grey.jpg\" width=\"2178\" height=\"2178\" />\n<p style=\"margin: 1em auto\">\nI am the <aa to=\"113\">unicorn who fell over</aa>.<br/>\nMy yelp called for <aa to=\"81\">rain</aa>.<br/>\nThe rain was a kind of a malaise.<br/>\nMy feelings as a unicorn are<br/>\ndistributed, and difficult to<br/>\nmeasure, but I will tell you<br/>\na secret about them. They<br/>\n(the best of fainting goats) are<br/>\ncontinuous with the natural world<br/>\nbecause they are a reversal of<br/>\nthe natural world. It is important<br/>\nthat you take better care of me,<br/>\nbecause I am economical and<br/>\ncontinuous with the natural<br/>\nworld and as real as a row of<br/>\nolive trees which need watering.\n</p>",
      "created": "2018-09-17T05:17:07.230Z",
      "fullWidth": false,
      "lovers": null,
      "page": 144,
      "parent": {
        "__v": 0,
        "_id": "5b9f322331175e004f00dd37",
        "background": "",
        "content": "<p>Look at this picture with me and imagine.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://codex-content.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/images/1537159961721-unicorns.png\" width=\"984\" height=\"635\"/>\n\n<p>\nThe spoiled lazy-bones pushed the unicorns too hard!<br/>\nTogether, they had spent hours trying to find a museum.<br/>\nThey wanted to become smarter.<br/>\nThe unicorns wanted to eat until they were full.</br>\nIt was a warm day which had cool breezes,<br/>\nlike those under a demonstrative sociocracy.<br/>\nThe unicorns with their spoiled lazy-bones<br/>\non top cantered right past the museum.\n</p>\n\n<p>There was something really lovely about the unicorns—<br/>\nit was undeniable, even if they had been pushed too hard.</p>\n\n<p>\nThe procession hit the highway, cantering around the cars,<br/>\nbarriers and construction equipment. If you could think<br/>\nof every possible way—and there are many—<br/>\nthat a thing with four spindles might canter down a highway<br/>\nin a big woven group, you wouldn't pick this way.<br/>\nYou'd pick something simpler and more likely to return,<br/>\nwhere the unicorn might move in an unmechanic<br/>\nsulk towards the slung balance of volumes, as if to<br/>\ntake into account the empty belly of the animal.\n</p>\n\n<p>This looked like a parade, but it wasn't.<br/>\nThey were actually trying to get somewhere.</p>\n\n<p>One unicorn fell down because it was so tired.<br/>\nIt yelped, which made the spoiled lazy-bone on top feel sad.</p>\n",
        "created": "2018-09-17T04:48:35.117Z",
        "fullWidth": false,
        "lovers": null,
        "page": 143,
        "parent": "5b861ecbf846b10050a621ef",
        "persons": null,
        "readme": "",
        "slug": "unicorns",
        "stub": false,
        "themes": [],
        "title": "Unicorns toiling",
        "word": []
      },
      "persons": null,
      "readme": "An engraving, hidden in the falling-down part of a museum of natural history, of a myotonic unicorn",
